WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.733 --> 00:00:01.901
♪ (ELECTRONIC MUSIC PLAYS) ♪

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.003
-GIRL:<i> Want to go
 on the Graviton?</i>
-RUE BENNETT:<i> Uh, no.</i>

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:05.338
-The Ferris wheel?
-Nope.

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.407
-Why?
-Because I don't wanna die.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.378
(SCREAMING, LAUGHTER)

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.281
SAM LEVINSON:<i> Episode four is</i>

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:17.784
<i> one of the more personal
 episodes of the show for me.</i>

00:00:19.451 --> 00:00:21.787 line:0%
When you're young and it's like,
the carnival's in town,

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:23.155 line:0%
it's always this major event,

00:00:23.255 --> 00:00:24.757
<i> and you know
 everyone's gonna be there.</i>

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.325
(GIGGLING)

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.928
MARCELL RÉV:<i> Sam had the idea
 to create a setting</i>

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:31.397
<i> that can be dreamy
 but based in reality,</i>

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:33.733 line:0%
and a small-time carnival
is a place like that.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:37.470 line:0%
It's essentially a somewhat
psychedelic or-- or like

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.807 line:0%
deeply experiential,
altered state that's going on.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.942
RÉV:
<i> Lots of colored, cool lights,</i>

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.444
you can imagine certain things
to happen there,

00:00:45.711 --> 00:00:47.713
<i> which won't happen
 in other places.</i>

00:00:48.313 --> 00:00:50.683
Hey. I'm really scared.

00:00:50.983 --> 00:00:52.252
Hands and feet inside the ride.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.854
(SCREAMING)

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:58.390
Marcel, myself and Peter Beck,
our storyboard artist, sat down

00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:01.327
<i> and basically storyboarded
 a carnival that didn't exist.</i>

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:03.696
<i> So, it was a massive thing
 to coordinate.</i>

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.266
They had essentially built
their own carnival.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:09.201
<i> They rented all the equipment,
 all the rides, everything.</i>

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:11.204
RÉV:<i> They built the carnival
 like two days</i>

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:14.007
<i> before we started shooting
 so we spent some time there,</i>

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:16.175
<i> figuring out shots,
 trying to adjust</i>

00:01:16.275 --> 00:01:18.344
our storyboards
to the actual location.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:22.649
LEVINSON:
<i> It was kind of conceived
 as an oblong-esque carnival</i>

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:26.051
in which we're able
to continually track through it.

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.354
So we could always be shooting
Rue something.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:30.489
<i> We could have foreground
 and background.</i>

00:01:30.589 --> 00:01:32.157
<i> We could utilize our extras
 in a way</i>

00:01:32.258 --> 00:01:34.127
<i>that gave it sort of real scope.</i>

00:01:35.128 --> 00:01:37.229
Welcome to Pretzelmania.
Can I take your order?

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:41.734
We started to shoot the carnival
with the smaller scenes,

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.569
<i> like the more intimate scenes.</i>

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:45.437
It was almost every single shot
was

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.940
<i>300 feet of dolly track we'd lay</i>

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:51.077
<i> and then we'd shoot a scene
 looking one way.</i>

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:52.278
<i> And then,
 we'd flip the dolly around</i>

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.413
<i> and shoot it the other way.</i>

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:57.216
So, we had like two days
while shooting after we wrapped,

00:01:57.316 --> 00:02:00.386
<i>the day we started to figure out
 this opening shot.</i>

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.189
Yeah. It's gonna be a good night
tonight, man.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:04.524
Let's get this money.

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:09.062
The concept was to create

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:11.397
a shot that connects
all the characters.

00:02:11.498 --> 00:02:14.033
You know, we had-- I think,
figured out a way

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:15.568
to weave through this thing

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.838
<i> and to really reveal the space
 step by step</i>

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.808
<i>with the characters and sort of
 see it with the characters.</i>

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:27.212
Sam wanted it to feel like
it was one shot, and it's not.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.582
We shot it, I think,
in five different pieces.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.417
JULIO PEREZ:
<i> You can look into it and see</i>

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:33.218
<i> where certain edit points
 might be,</i>

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:34.787
<i> but it's very hard to find it.</i>

00:02:34.887 --> 00:02:36.522
LEVINSON:<i> The design
 of the entire carnival</i>

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:39.491
was how can we achieve
everything in these single shots

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.427
<i> so we can feel the flow of it.</i>

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:44.330
PEREZ:<i> The material was like
coming in, and we'd look at it,</i>

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.867
just like-- going like,
"Wow, this shot is phenomenal."

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:50.169
RÉV:<i> It's a tough thing
 for everyone to create</i>

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.171
a technically complicated shot
like that,

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:54.607
<i> but yeah,
 they did a really great job.</i>

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.709
♪ (MUSIC CONCLUDES) ♪

